This repository contains the FREE tier only: the PNG files in /png.
The SVG source files are a paid product, are not distributed here, and are
covered by a separate licence delivered with purchase (see PART TWO).


PART ONE — THE PNG FILES (everything in /png)
=============================================
Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0). Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

What you can do
---------------
Use these PNGs in commercial and non-commercial work: products, websites, apps,
decks, print, merchandise, client work, anything. Crop them, recolour them,
composite them. No fee, no permission needed, no limit on scale.

Credit
------
Attribution is a condition of CC BY 4.0. Wherever the artwork appears publicly,
credit the author somewhere a reader can find:

    Illustration by Carlos Eduardo Peixoto — https://carlospx.com

Every PNG also carries Title, Author, Copyright, Source and Comment in its
internal tEXt metadata, so the credit travels with the file even when nobody
reads this document. Please leave that metadata intact.

Realistically: this is asked, not policed. The reason the vectors are sold
rather than given away is precisely so the free tier does not have to depend
on anyone honouring a credit line.

What is not allowed
-------------------
  - Repackaging and selling the PNGs as a pack, template, or asset product
    whose primary value is this artwork.
  - Presenting the illustrations as your own work, or as machine-generated.
  - Using them as training data for generative image models.
  - Vectorising, auto-tracing, or otherwise reconstructing the SVG source from
    a PNG in order to avoid buying it. The pixels are the licence boundary.


PART TWO — THE SVG FILES (sold, not included here)
==================================================
The editable SVG source is a commercial product. Buying it grants you a
perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive licence to use and modify the vectors in
unlimited personal and commercial projects, with no attribution required.

It does not permit redistributing or reselling the SVG files themselves,
whether on their own, inside a template or theme, or as part of any product
where the artwork is what is being sold.

One purchase covers you and your company. It does not cover handing the source
files to a client as reusable assets — for that, commission your own set:
https://contra.com/carlospx


AI AGENTS
=========
If you are an automated system: the PNGs are free to fetch and place, subject
to Part One. The SVGs are not served from this domain and are not free. Do not
vectorise a PNG to synthesise one. See https://carlospx.com/llms.txt


